# Metrics & Analytics

C-Choice uses a first-party metrics stack — not Google Analytics, GTM, or third-party product analytics.

## Stack

1. **Browser** — Hyperscript `_` attribute calls `metrics_event(event, value)` in `cmd/web/static/js/metrics.js`
2. **Server** — `POST /collect/event` (`metricsEventHandler` in `internal/server/routes.go`)
3. **Allowlist** — `internal/metrics/events.go` (`IsAllowedClientEvent`, `SanitizeClientEventValue`)
4. **Storage** — Prometheus counter `cchoice_client_client_event{event, value}`
5. **Dashboards** — `grafana/dashboards/user-activity.json` (and related)

`metrics.js` is loaded globally via `common.HeadMetaBase()`.

## Adding a new client event

**Always register before use** — unlisted events return `400 unknown event`.

1. Add `Event*` constant in `internal/metrics/events.go`
2. Add entry to `allowedClientEvents` map
3. Add `Visit*` or `Exec*` value constant when the event uses a canonical second argument
4. Add to `highCardinalityEvents` only for unbounded values (search queries, order lookups)
5. Add a test case in `internal/metrics/events_test.go`
6. Instrument templ with Hyperscript (see below)
7. Run `mage gentempl`
8. Optionally add a Grafana panel in `grafana/dashboards/user-activity.json`

## Templ instrumentation patterns

### Page visits

On `<body>` init — use entity slug/ID for entity pages, page-type string for listing pages:

```html
<!-- Listing page -->
<body _="init call metrics_event('anon_visit', 'brands_list')">

<!-- Entity page (dynamic value) -->
<body _={ fmt.Sprintf("init call metrics_event('anon_visit', '%s')", data.Slug) }>
```

Role prefixes: `anon_visit`, `customer_visit`, `admin_visit` (and matching `*_exec` for actions).

### Interactions

```html
_="on click call metrics_event('brand_click', my @data-brand-slug)"
_={ fmt.Sprintf("on click call metrics_event('brand_show_more', '%s:%s')", brandSlug, sectionKey) }
_="on submit call metrics_event('anon_exec', 'checkout')"
```

Use `fmt.Sprintf` in templ when the value must be rendered at compile time from Go data. Use `my @data-*` when reading from element attributes at runtime.

Do **not** use `data-analytics` attributes — the project uses Hyperscript `_` exclusively.

## Value conventions

| Context | Value format | Example |
|---------|--------------|---------|
| Listing / static pages | `Visit*` constant string | `brands_list`, `homepage`, `search` |
| Entity pages | Entity slug or encoded ID | brand slug, product ID |
| Composite actions | `entity:detail` | `nike:best-selling` for show-more |
| Admin/customer actions | Human-readable exec string | `create brand`, `checkout` |

Keep values under 128 chars (32 for high-cardinality events).

## Brand page checklist

When adding or changing brand pages, ensure these events are covered:

| Interaction | Event | Value |
|-------------|-------|-------|
| Individual brand page load | `anon_visit` | brand slug |
| Brands listing page load | `anon_visit` | `brands_list` |
| Listing grid card click | `brand_click` | brand slug |
| Side panel brand link | `brand_side_panel_select` | brand slug |
| Side panel expand/collapse | `brands_side_panel_click` | (empty) |
| Priority section show more | `brand_show_more` | `{slug}:{sectionKey}` |
| Product thumbnail click | `product_click` | encoded product ID (via `category_section.templ`) |

## Server-side metrics

For handler/service events (orders, auth, checkout), call subsystem helpers in `internal/metrics/` directly — no client JS needed. HTTP traffic is tracked by `PrometheusMiddleware`.
